.TH HTOP_PLUS 1 "2026" "htop_plus" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
htop_plus \- interactive process viewer with NVIDIA and power cable meters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htop_plus
.RI [ htop-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
htop_plus extends htop with NVIDIA GPU sensors, Docker-aware process
usernames, and a read-only WINGSTUDIO 12V-2X6 Ti cable meter.
The USER column displays Docker owners as [container-name]container-user.
The NVIDIA meter shows usage, used/total VRAM in K/M/G, temperature,
fan percentage/RPM, and power in watts.
The external cable meter shows six voltage/current/power channels,
total cable power on a 1000W display scale, connector temperature (Con),
and controller temperature (Ctl).
The 1000W scale does not measure total PSU power or configure hardware limits.
.PP
Cable readings come from the nvpowermon 2.0.1 service over a read-only
Unix socket subscription. Multiple monitoring clients can run concurrently.
Only the service accesses the serial device and reads its configuration.
Disconnected, invalid or stale readings show N/A; reconnection is retried
every five seconds. Samples expire ten seconds after the service query.
.PP
Press F2 to configure meters and columns; press F10 or q to quit.
Run htop_plus --help for the full list of supported htop command-line options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --readonly
Disable process-changing operations.
.TP
.B --version
Display the htop_plus name and underlying htop version.
.TP
.B --help
Display all supported command-line options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HTOPRC
Override the user interface configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
User configuration directory, defaulting to $HOME/.config.
Installed htop_plus creates htop_plus/htoprc here on first run.
Existing layouts are preserved during startup and upgrades.
.TP
.B HTOP_POWER_CABLE_SOCKET
Override /run/nvpowermon/status.sock, or set to off to disable cable readings.
The path must be absolute.
.TP
.B NVPOWERMON_SOCKET
Shared socket override, used when HTOP_POWER_CABLE_SOCKET is unset or empty.
.TP
.B HTOP_POWER_CABLE_PORT
The legacy value off still disables readings. Other port overrides and
HTOP_POWER_CABLE_CONFIG are retired; configure the nvpowermon service instead.
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Select a local Docker socket using unix:///path/to/docker.sock.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/htop_plus/htoprc
Per-user meter layout, independent of the original htop configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/nvpowermon/config.json
Device connection settings read by the nvpowermon service, not this client.
.TP
.I /run/nvpowermon/status.sock
Default nvpowermon subscription socket (protocol v1).
.SH NOTES
The installer places the native executable at /usr/local/bin/htop_plus
by default. The process name and executable basename are both htop_plus.
It does not replace the system htop executable.
Upgrades remove the previous libexec/htop_plus/htop executable.
The source checkout binary keeps its layout in the source directory.
Install nvpowermon separately and register its service with
sudo nvpowermon --register. For an existing service, use
sudo nvpowermon --start and nvpowermon --status.
